==============================================================================
  5  Perplexity, and where an untrained model must start
==============================================================================
  vocabulary V                      : 50,257
  ln(V), the uniform-guess loss     : 10.8249
  measured loss, untrained model    : 10.9289
  measured perplexity               : 55,764
  ratio perplexity / V              : 1.110
  excess over ln(V)                 : +0.1040

  It lands just ABOVE ln(V), and it has to. ln(V) is the loss of a model that is exactly
  uniform; any spread in the initial logits is confidence the model has not earned, and on
  a random target unearned confidence costs more than it saves. The excess is a direct
  measure of how opinionated the initialisation is.

