==============================================================================
  1  Every tensor shape, and what each dimension means
==============================================================================
  tokens          (4, 256)                B sequences x T positions; each entry is one token id
  hidden          (4, 256, 384)           B x T x D; one D-vector per position, having seen its whole left context
  lm_head.weight  (50257, 384)            V rows x D; one learned row per vocabulary token
  logits          (4, 256, 50257)         B x T x V; one raw score per vocabulary token, per position
  inputs          (4, 255)                B x (T-1); the last position is dropped -- nothing follows it
  targets         (4, 255)                B x (T-1); the first token is dropped -- nothing predicts it
  flat logits     (1020, 50257)           (B*(T-1)) x V; cross_entropy wants one row per prediction
  flat targets    (1020,)                 (B*(T-1)); one correct token id per prediction

  B=4  T=256  D=384  V=50,257
  logits tensor is 131x larger than the hidden state that produced it

